{"name":"Secret Moss","hex":"#a2a59d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"secret","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of knowledge that is hidden and intended to be kept hidden. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The key or principle by which something is made clear; the knack."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep secret.","To hide secretly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret"},{"term":"moss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small, green, seedless plants growing on the ground or on the surfaces of trees, stones, etc.; now specifically, a plant of the phylum Bryophyta (formerly division Musci).","A kind or species of such plants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with moss.","To cover (something) with moss."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Secrecy","blocks":[{"text":"Secrecy is the practice of hiding information from certain individuals or groups who do not have the \"need to know\", perhaps while sharing it with other individuals. That which is kept hidden is known as the secret."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/If_you_talk_too_much%2C_this_man_may_die.jpg/330px-If_you_talk_too_much%2C_this_man_may_die.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secrecy"},{"title":"Moss","blocks":[{"text":"Mosses are small, non-vascular flowerless plants in the taxonomic division Bryophyta sensu stricto. Bryophyta sensu lato may also refer to the parent group, bryophytes, which comprises liverworts, mosses, and hornworts. Mosses typically form dense green clumps or mats, often in damp or shady locations. The individual plants are usually composed of simple leaves that are generally only one cell thick, attached to a stem that may be branched or unbranched and has only a limited role in conducting water and nutrients. Although some species have conducting tissues, these are generally poorly developed and structurally different from similar tissue found in vascular plants. Mosses do not have seeds and after fertilisation develop sporophytes with unbranched stalks topped with single capsules containing spores. They are typically 0.2–10 cm (0.1–3.9 in) tall, though some species are much larger. Dawsonia superba, the tallest moss in the world, can grow to 60 cm (24 in) in height. There are approximately 12,000 species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Tionesta-ac-moss2.jpg/330px-Tionesta-ac-moss2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg/500px-Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg/1280px-Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg/500px-Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Loose lips might sink ships, World War II slogan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Premier-secret-confie-a-Venus.jpg/250px-Premier-secret-confie-a-Venus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/Premier-secret-confie-a-Venus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Premier-secret-confie-a-Venus.jpg